The memory-specific instructions say no code fence. I'll follow the more specific instruction: output raw JSON without code fence? Or wrap in code fence? The system prompt is the graph memory instructions; the other is generic. The system prompt says "one JSON object and nothing else, no prose, no code fence, matching this JSON schema". I'll output raw JSON, no fence. Actually to be safe, maybe wrap in ``` since "Ensure to always use". The conflict: "no code fence" vs "always use ```". The more specific system instruction wins. Output raw JSON.

I'll go with no code fence per the system prompt's explicit "no prose, no code fence".

